<title>ISRAEL: Bank of Israel intervenes to support basket.</title>
<headline>Bank of Israel intervenes to support basket.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Israel intervened several times in shekel trading on Monday, buying foreign currency to support the sagging basket of foreign currencies, dealers at commercial banks said.</p>
<p>&quot;The central bank intervened many times and on a higher scale than in the last few days,&quot; a dealer at Bank Hapoalim said. He estimated the central bank bought about $100 million worth of foreign currency.</p>
</text>
